G.2.1.2 Circular Polyline

Circular Polyline is a line that contains at least one circular curve segment. The curve segment connects two adjacent
points by a circular arc. The curve segment is determined by the two adjacent points and a curve offset (the
perpendicular distance from the center of the line connecting the adjacent points to the circular arc).

